    "body": "## Context & Problem Statement\nYield-bearing assets deposited in the vault currently require manual harvesting. An auto-compounding strategy maximizes APY for vault share holders while distributing a small bounty to incentivize external callers to trigger compounding.\n\n## Proposed Solution & Implementation Steps\n1. Update `contracts/yield/src/lib.rs` to track vault share supply and user share balances using the ERC-4626 vault pattern.\n2. Implement `harvest()` function that collects accrued yield from underlying staking pools.\n3. Deduct a configurable performance fee (e.g. 2%) sent to revenue distributor, and a caller bounty (e.g. 0.5%) sent to the caller.\n4. Reinvest remaining yield into the principal pool, minting proportional vault shares.\n5. Add integration tests covering deposit, harvest compounding, and withdrawal round-trip.\n\n## Contributor Workflow Guide\n- **Branch:** `feat/issue-{ISSUE_NUMBER}-vault-auto-compounding`\n- **Commit Convention:** `feat(contracts/vault): implement ERC-4626 auto-compounding vault with harvest bounty`\n- **PR Type:** `Feature`\n- **PR Submission Checklist:**\n  - [ ] References `Closes #{ISSUE_NUMBER}`\n  - [ ] Includes share pricing calculation tests\n  - [ ] Verified harvest fee distribution math\n  - [ ] Code passes all linting, formatting, and type checks\n  - [ ] No sensitive credentials or secrets committed (verified via secretlint)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Harvest operation compounds yield into principal balance.\n- [ ] Caller bounty rewards external automation bots.\n- [ ] Share price increases monotonically over compounding cycles.",
